# Gameplay C#

Assemblies: `Tumble.Simulation`, `Tumble.Presentation`, `Tumble.App`. Simulation does not reference presentation, UI, or the Input System.

```csharp
// Motor step. No input, no Time.time, no camera.
public void Simulate(PlayerCommand command, RoundClock clock, float dt)
{
    if (command.JumpPressed && CanJump(clock))
        StartJump();
}
```

- Match file name to the type. One main type per file.
- Profile fields replace numeric literals for anything listed in `docs/game-feel.md`.
- `MotorState` keeps the explicit values in `docs/contracts.md`.
- Events notify presentation. Subscribers do not write velocity or qualification.
- Edit Mode tests cover pure command logic. Feel is checked with the spec's Gym checklist.
